From: Martin Jungblut Schreiner <martin.schreiner@suse.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix bundled Python packaging on 32-bit x86 and s390x

external/python3/ExternalPackage_python3.mk hand-derives two platform tuples
and lacks branches for s390x and 32-bit x86 in both:

1. SOABI, used for python3_EXTENSION_MODULE_SUFFIX (the .so existence check).
   Only AARCH64 and POWERPC64 are handled; CPUNAME=INTEL and CPUNAME=S390X
   fall through to the x86_64 default, so the build looks for e.g.
   array.cpython-312-x86_64-linux-gnu.so while Python emits the -i386- or
   -s390x- suffixed file.

2. The generated _sysconfigdata file under LO_lib/. powerpc64le and aarch64
   have explicit branches; every other platform uses the HOST_PLATFORM
   fallback, which only strips a "-pc" vendor. s390x's HOST_PLATFORM is
   s390x-ibm-linux-gnu, so the "-pc" substitution is a no-op and the build
   requests _sysconfigdata__linux_s390x-ibm-linux-gnu.py, whereas CPython
   generates it as _sysconfigdata__linux_s390x-linux-gnu.py (its MULTIARCH
   carries no vendor field). The build aborts with
   "file ..._sysconfigdata__linux_s390x-ibm-linux-gnu.py does not exist in
   the tarball."

Add the missing INTEL and S390X SOABI branches, and an explicit s390x
sysconfigdata branch mirroring the existing aarch64 one.

--- a/external/python3/ExternalPackage_python3.mk	2026-05-24 13:36:45.713158620 +0000
+++ b/external/python3/ExternalPackage_python3.mk	2026-05-24 13:36:59.353830700 +0000
@@ -70,6 +70,10 @@
 SOABI=-aarch64-linux-gnu
 else ifeq ($(CPUNAME),POWERPC64)
 SOABI=-powerpc64le-linux-gnu
+else ifeq ($(CPUNAME),S390X)
+SOABI=-s390x-linux-gnu
+else ifeq ($(CPUNAME),INTEL)
+SOABI=-i386-linux-gnu
 else
 SOABI=-x86_64-linux-gnu
 endif
@@ -163,6 +167,11 @@
         LO_lib/_sysconfigdata_$(if $(ENABLE_DBGUTIL),d)_linux_aarch64-linux-gnu.py \
 ))
 else
+ifeq ($(HOST_PLATFORM),s390x-ibm-linux-gnu)
+$(eval $(call gb_ExternalPackage_add_files,python3,$(LIBO_BIN_FOLDER)/python-core-$(PYTHON_VERSION)/lib,\
+        LO_lib/_sysconfigdata_$(if $(ENABLE_DBGUTIL),d)_linux_s390x-linux-gnu.py \
+))
+else
 # note: python configure overrides config.guess with something that doesn't
 # put -pc in its linux platform triplets, so filter that...
 ifneq ($(OS),WNT)
@@ -177,6 +186,7 @@
 endif
 endif
 endif
+endif
 endif
 
 
